Gates: DEPENDENCY_GATE

Spec: DependencyGate

Purpose:
  The intake APPROVE/REJECT decision gate for every NEW dependency
  (library, package, module, service client). A dependency is added
  to the project ONLY after this gate passes. Scanners
  (security/scanners.sdd SEC.DEP) detect known risk; THIS gate
  decides BEFORE the dependency enters the codebase.

Owns: gates/dependency-gate.sdd

Scope:
  New direct dependencies proposed during any stage (TK task
  breakdown, unit implementation, RF refactor). Version bumps of
  already-approved dependencies are out of scope unless the major
  version changes (then re-gate).

GateFlow (each check MUST be answered before the next):

  request            New dependency proposed (name, version, reason)
     |
  necessity          WHY — capability cannot be met by existing code?
     |
  existing           Does an already-approved dependency provide it?
     |
  stdlib             Is the standard library sufficient?
     |
  maintenance        Actively maintained? release cadence, bus factor,
                     security history (past advisories, response time)
     |
  cve                Known advisories for this version? (scanner-
                     backed: snyk / npm-audit / grype — SEC.DEP)
     |
  transitive        What else does it pull? blast radius = dependency
                     tree size + surface of each transitive hop
     |
  license            Compatible with the project license?
     |
  security_impact    Attack surface: network, auth, secret handling,
                     eval/dynamic code, native bindings
     |
  APPROVE | REJECT   Reason recorded in the task's decision trail

Decision:
  APPROVE — all checks green; entry recorded with evidence.
  REJECT  — any HARD-FAIL check (below) fails; proposal recorded
            with the failing check and reason.
  DEFER   — evidence unavailable (offline sandbox): proposal
            parked as an ASSUMPTION (assumptions/ registry) and
            the dependency is NOT added until evidence exists.

HardFail (any of these => REJECT, no override):
  - CVE CRITICAL or HIGH open for the proposed version
  - License incompatible or copyleft-obligation without human
    approval (GPL-family) [DG5]
  - Unmaintained: no release or security response for 12+ months
  - Unaudited provenance (no source repo, no checksum) [DG5]

Rules:

  [DG1] No APPROVE => the dependency MUST NOT be added: AI MUST NOT
        install, import, or vendor it.
  [DG2] APPROVE/REJECT reasons are recorded in the task's decision
        trail (DEC record or task record) — traceable audit [GT8].
  [DG3] The gate result carries Condition + Evidence + Threshold +
        Owner + Decision [GT3].
  [DG4] Scanner evidence (SEC.DEP) attaches to the CVE and
        transitive checks; findings CRITICAL/HIGH force REJECT.
  [DG5] Human approval is REQUIRED for: GPL-family/obligation
        licenses, unaudited provenance, and any native-code
        dependency. AI cannot waive ([G11] applies).
  [DG6] DEPENDENCY_GATE runs BEFORE implementation of the unit that
        needs it ([SB7]) — never retroactively after `install`.
  [DG7] The declared dependency list lives in the task record;
        CR-XX diffs against it — an undeclared new dependency fails
        the review (bax ../workflow/step-keys.sdd CRScopedSemantics).

EvidenceFormat:

  DEPENDENCY_GATE
  dependency: <name>@<version>
  requested_by: SUBTASK-<id> | TASK-<id>
  checks:
    necessity: PASS|FAIL — <reason>
    existing:  PASS|FAIL — <reason>
    stdlib:    PASS|FAIL — <reason>
    maintenance: PASS|FAIL — <reason>
    cve:       PASS|FAIL — <scanner evidence id>
    transitive: PASS|FAIL — <tree size, notable hops>
    license:   PASS|FAIL|HUMAN — <license id>
    security_impact: PASS|FAIL — <surface notes>
  decision: APPROVE | REJECT | DEFER
  owner: <stage/role>
  recorded: <timestamp> + decision trail reference

Navigation:
  GatesIndex: @INDEX.sdd
  Scanners: @../security/scanners.sdd (SEC.DEP)
  StageGates: @stage/gates.sdd (SC gate cites this gate)
  Stages: @../workflow/stages.sdd (TK exit criterion)
  StepKeys: @../workflow/step-keys.sdd (CR-XX dependency diff)
  SubtaskSchema: @../schemas/subtask.sdd ([SB7])
  Assumptions: @../assumptions/INDEX.sdd (DEFER path)

State: +
  (Phase 155: created as the missing intake gate between the
   scanner catalog (detection) and the dependency graph engine
   (representation); enforces security-first ordering [R101] —
   dependencies are decided, never spontaneously added)
